        "execSummary":  "The governance-versus-speed tension has become the defining leadership question of enterprise AI in mid-2026, and this piece offers a practical framing for CIOs navigating it without defaulting to either extreme. The emerging answer is tiered governance ΓÇö high oversight for customer-facing and high-stakes AI, lighter-touch for internal productivity tools ΓÇö rather than a blanket policy. For customer-support and operations leaders, this distinction matters directly: autonomous AI handling customer escalations demands a different accountability model than an internal summarization tool. The risk of over-indexing on innovation speed is not just regulatory ΓÇö it is reputational, as failures in customer-facing AI are public and immediate.",
